{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "28ffa725-4097-45bf-9303-4b8e390a1327",
    "name": "equis.session-templates",
    "description": "Riding Schedule \u2014 E2 session templates (W1 admin) against equis-api: list, create, edit and delete under /admin/session-templates.\n\nBefore running:\n1. Dev database with V1\u2013V9 applied. Level 3 must have no Wednesday or Friday templates of its own, or the overlap checks will see extra warnings.\n2. Set adminEmail and adminPassword. Prefer a Postman environment so the password isn't saved in the collection.\n\nRun order: 0 \u2192 4. The collection creates three templates and deletes them again in folder 4. Deletes are soft, so the rows and their cancelled sessions stay in the database.\nNot covered here: booked-seat counts and the capacity_exceeded conflict (bookings do not exist yet, so every count is 0).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 \u00b7 Sign in",
      "description": "Run first: every other request uses adminAccessToken.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Admin login \u2192 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Saves adminAccessToken (valid for 15 minutes).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"login\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\",\n  \"rememberMe\": false\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"role = ADMIN\", () => pm.expect(b.role).to.eql(\"ADMIN\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminAccessToken\", b.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 \u00b7 List (W1 tabs)",
      "description": "GET with level = a level number (1\u20136) or \"assessment\". Anything else is a 400.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Level 1 tab \u2192 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/session-templates?level=1",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "session-templates"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "level",
                  "value": "1"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "A fresh dev database has two seeded level 1 templates (V8)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const list = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Is an array\", () => pm.expect(list).to.be.an(\"array\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Only level 1\", () => list.forEach(t => pm.expect(t.levelId).to.eql(1)));",
                  "pm.test(\"Times are HH:mm\", () => list.forEach(t => { pm.expect(t.start).to.match(/^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$/); pm.expect(t.end).to.match(/^\\d{2}:\\d{2}$/); }));",
                  "pm.test(\"Each row has both counts\", () => list.forEach(t => { pm.expect(t.maxBookedInUpcoming).to.be.a(\"number\"); pm.expect(t.bookingsInUpcoming).to.be.a(\"number\"); }));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
